{"id":"HKF-128","kind":"appraisal","key":"D06","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Section VIII.B averages latency over N=100 sequential tasks and evaluates sensitivity across node counts (4–20), heights (20–100 m), models, and quantization scales (0.1–0.6), but omits variance, confidence intervals, or multi-trial dispersion.","evidence":[{"page":11,"section":"VIII.B Overall Performance","quote":"The average latency is measured by dividing the"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-128","kind":"appraisal","key":"D07","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Deployed on 24 Jetson boards over WiFi and 5 real-world UAVs with Ad-hoc modules plus cluster-head cut-off/recovery tests, but flight trajectories, speeds, outdoor distances, and channel fading statistics are not reported.","evidence":[{"page":11,"section":"VIII.A Evaluation Setup","quote":"the UAVs transmit data through the Ad hoc"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-128","kind":"appraisal","key":"D08","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Sections IX and X align conclusions with measured testbed results, explicitly noting ASAP targets single-task-flow inference (not RL training) and recommending future work on optimal UAV counts and volatile-network fault tolerance.","evidence":[{"page":15,"section":"IX. DISCUSSION","quote":"The proposed system mainly considers the situation of"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-128","kind":"appraisal","key":"D09","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Sections I and VII explicitly open-source the 4,000+ line Python ASAP implementation at https://github.com/snhao222/ASAP; CIFAR-10 and custom video source data are also described (link not externally fetched).","evidence":[{"page":9,"section":"VII. IMPLEMENTATION","quote":"we have open sourced our work at https:"}],"note":""}
