{"id":"HKF-128","kind":"outcome","key":"Q02","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"Observed metric: latency across node scale (4–20 Jetson Nano, 720x1280, N=100); prose prints ResNet152 43.1% reduction (20 vs 4 nodes) and rebound for ResNet101 at 20 nodes and ResNet50 at 16 nodes; Table III cells unreadable.","evidence":[{"page":11,"section":"VIII.B Overall Performance","quote":"ResNet101 and ResNet50 rebounds again when the number"}],"note":"Table III numeric entries on p. 12 are missing in PDFKit text."}
{"id":"HKF-128","kind":"report_coverage","key":"coverage","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PRINTED_UNRESOLVED: Checked §§I, VIII.B–E, X (pp. 3, 11–15). Prose prints exact relative reductions (e.g., 43.1%, 92.66%, 95.35%, 98.50%, 87.2%~92.7%), but Tables III–V cells and Figs. 13–18 values are unextracted/plot-only in PDFKit text.","evidence":[{"page":12,"section":"VIII.B Overall Performance","quote":"ASAP can reduce the computing latency by up"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-128","kind":"technical","key":"t2_decisions_objective_solver","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Decisions: inter-cluster model split, intra-cluster data range, adaptive quantization scale. Objective: minimize pipeline/cluster max-latency (make l1=...=lM/lN) with bounded accuracy loss. Solver: heuristic MRT+ICLB+ECLB+ES with operator-level+16-neuron fusion predictor. Missing: formal energy/bandwidth constraints.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"IV.A Inter-Cluster Load Balancing","quote":"the collaborative latency of a task in a"},{"page":7,"section":"IV.B Intra-Cluster Load Balancing","quote":"the ECLB algorithm adjusts the submodels for each"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-128","kind":"technical","key":"t2_partition","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Two-level hybrid partitioning: DL model partitioned sequentially across UAV clusters (pipeline parallel via ECLB); input feature maps partitioned spatially within each cluster (data parallel via MRT+ICLB with custom zero-padding). Intermediate tensors quantized to 8-bit+gzip.","evidence":[{"page":4,"section":"III. SYSTEM OVERVIEW","quote":"The model is partitioned among UAV clusters and"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-128","kind":"technical","key":"t2_topology","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Hierarchical clustered UAV relay swarm without base stations. Task-publisher UAV runs external model-partition scheduler; cluster-head UAVs relay inter-cluster data, run internal data-partition scheduler, and monitor state; cluster members execute local data partitions.","evidence":[{"page":9,"section":"VII.A System Module Design","quote":"The task scheduler of task publisher UAV controls"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-128","kind":"technical","key":"t2_workload","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Models: VGG16, ResNet34, DarkNet19 (medium); ResNet50, ResNet101, ResNet152 (large). Data: video at 720x1280, 540x960, 180x320; CIFAR-10 for compression. Baselines: raw offloading, Neurosurgeon, DeepSlicing, MoDNN, onboard, average scheduler, FLOPs predictor, nn-Meter. Missing: source video identity.","evidence":[{"page":11,"section":"VIII.A Evaluation Setup","quote":"We evaluate the performance of ASAP with 3"}],"note":""}
