{"id":"HKF-013","kind":"appraisal","key":"D03","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Section IV.A specifies three SBC profiles (Raspberry Pi 3B+, Orange Pi Zero, Odroid with f=560, 480, 307.2), three CNNs, beta=0.7, gamma=0.3, and rho=72.2 Mbps, but omits energy budgets Emax, power P, v0, N, S, simulator, and dataset.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"IV.A Simulation Settings","quote":"equal to 560 for Raspberry Pi 3B+, 480"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-013","kind":"appraisal","key":"D04","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"YES: Section IV.A–B compares EECIA against four baselines (Random, Nearest, DistInference, OPT) under shared CNNs (AlexNet, ResNet152, VGG-16), UAV counts (3–10), and data rates, noting OPT times out for VGG-16 at I=10.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"IV.A Simulation Settings","quote":"We introduce four benchmark algorithms Random, Nearest, DistInference"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-013","kind":"appraisal","key":"D05","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Evaluation directly measures the primary objective (total inference latency Ttot) and solver runtime (Table II), but does not report UAV energy consumption or energy-constraint satisfaction despite framing the work as energy-efficient.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"IV.B Results Analysis","quote":"Table. II shows the running time of these"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-013","kind":"appraisal","key":"D06","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Section IV.B evaluates sensitivity across CNN models (Fig. 3), data rates (Fig. 4), and UAV counts 3–8 (Fig. 5), but does not report number of trials/repetitions, random seeds, or variance/error bars.","evidence":[{"page":7,"section":"IV.B Results Analysis","quote":"we research the impact of the number of"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-013","kind":"appraisal","key":"D07","status":"NO","finding":"NO: Section IV.A explicitly simplifies the wireless channel to a constant data rate per inference request with full all-to-all reachability and no UAV mobility, fading, interference, or link failure; Section V defers dynamic networks to future work.","evidence":[{"page":6,"section":"IV.A Simulation Settings","quote":"we assume that all devices are not isolated"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-013","kind":"appraisal","key":"D08","status":"PARTIAL","finding":"PARTIAL: Latency and runtime claims match simulations, but Section V claims to perform classification tasks 'accurately' and 'energy-efficient' despite never evaluating classification accuracy or reporting measured energy consumption.","evidence":[{"page":7,"section":"V. CONCLUSION","quote":"We can quickly and accurately perform classification tasks"}],"note":""}
